{
  "name": "louse",
  "_about": "The head louse (Pediculus humanus capitis), 3 mm long: flat, wingless and greyish, half translucent; a small head with short five-jointed antennae and tiny dark eyes; a squat thorax; a long oval abdomen with dark plates along its lobed edges and the last blood meal showing through as a red-brown blur; three pairs of stout legs, each ending in one big claw that closes on a hair. Coat: unfed (pale). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/bugs.py on insectlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
